    "result_text": "All 34 tests pass with **BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the GOLD membership tier: an owner's `membershipTier` is now `'GOLD'` when their household (owners sharing the same `householdId`) has 3+ members after the create; otherwise the existing SILVER/BRONZE rules apply.\n\nFollowing the established pattern for `namesakeCount` \u2014 a snapshot count computed during the create pipeline, persisted on the entity, and read by the mapper at response time \u2014 I made these changes:\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `householdMemberCount` field (`household_member_count` column) with getter/setter.\n\n2. **`AssignHouseholdMemberCount.java`** (new pipeline step) \u2014 after `AssignHouseholdId` has assigned and back-filled the shared `householdId` but before save, it counts owners sharing that `householdId` plus the not-yet-saved new owner (1 when the owner isn't in a shared household).\n\n3. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the new step in between `assignHousehold` and `assignNamesakeCount`, under the same `transaction` governance.\n\n4. **`OwnerMapper.membershipTier`** \u2014 returns `GOLD` when `householdMemberCount >= 3`, otherwise falls through to the unchanged SILVER/BRONZE logic.\n\n5. **Schema files** (hsqldb, h2, postgres, mysql) \u2014 added the `household_member_count` column; and **hsqldb `data.sql`** \u2014 added the extra trailing `NULL` to each positional seed INSERT (the other DBs use column-named inserts and needed no change).\n\n6. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `membershipTier` description to document the GOLD rule.\n\nThe snapshot approach matches the spec's create-time-anchored wording (\"has 3 or more members after this create\") and is consistent with how `namesakeCount` and `bulkSignupWarning` already work. Existing/seed owners with a null count fall through to SILVER/BRONZE, so the change is backward compatible.",
